  "body": "Sibling of #4944, left open by its fix (7fc781e1e on the gg-ship stack, ported from ggbdpq's patch).\n\n#4944's fix is in `chatTidy`: a Chat stream relayed to a Chat client whose finish is `\"tool_calls\"` with no call in it now ends `stop`. The translated route has the same hole. When a Chat upstream ends with `finish_reason: \"tool_calls\"` and sends no call, and the client speaks Anthropic Messages or Responses, `collector.finish` (`internal/gateway/ir.go`) keeps `Stop == \"tool\"`: it only turns `stop` into `tool` when a ToolCall part exists, never `tool` back into `stop` when none does. The client then gets `stop_reason: \"tool_use\"` (or a Responses turn waiting on a call) with no tool block, and an agent waits for a call that never comes, as Hermes did in #4944.\n\nExpected: a reply with no ToolCall part ends `stop` whatever finish the upstream named, as the Chat→Chat route now does. Test: a Chat upstream streaming text then `finish_reason: \"tool_calls\"` with no `tool_calls` delta, asked through `/v1/messages` and `/v1/responses`; the reply's stop is end_turn / completed, with no tool block.\n\nFound while reviewing #4944's patch; not fixed there because that patch is scoped to chatTidy.\n",
