   "created_at": "2026-11-08T21:24:03Z",
   "updated_at": "2026-11-08T21:24:03Z",
   "body": "A fix is on [the fork branch](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/5376-translated-phantom-tool-finish), commit [12cd2055f](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/12cd2055fc464c6edc9dc10262ab4b8752a60e20), based on `ed0ab567`.\n\nThe shared collector now resolves a `tool` finish from the actual tool-call parts. Text-only Chat replies ending `tool_calls` therefore reach Messages clients as `end_turn`, without a phantom tool block. Real tool calls still finish as tools; length/filter reasons are preserved.\n\nA real local HTTP gateway with a fake Chat upstream reproduces the Messages failure for both whole and streamed replies before the fix and passes afterwards. The Responses whole/stream controls already passed on the base, so I am not claiming an additional Responses wire failure. Reverting the condition makes both Messages cases fail again. Parent verification passed these cases and existing real-tool controls under `-race`; gateway vet, formatting and the full `nogui` build passed. No live provider or full test suite was run. AI-assisted implementation and review.",
